examples/.rumoca/results/
rumoca_trace*.csv

# **The HRW bridge directory, at the ROOT as well as under `hrw/`.**
#
# `hrw/.gitignore` already carries `/.hrw-bridge`, and that anchor covers only
# `hrw/`. HRW itself always writes to `hrw/.hrw-bridge/` — `bridge.rs` builds every
# path from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`, not from the working directory — so the app cannot
# produce one here. **A scratch specimen written by hand from the workspace root
# can**, and two were on 2026-11-03: they landed in an unignored `.hrw-bridge/` and
# showed up in `git status` as the only untracked entry in the tree.
#
# `bridge.rs` says scratch probes are "ephemeral by construction" because they live
# under a gitignored directory. That is true of the path HRW builds and not of the
# string `.hrw-bridge/specimens/…`, so this line makes the claim hold either way.
/.hrw-bridge

